# PAM configuration for veiland's password check (Debian/Ubuntu).
# Authenticate only: no account, session, or password phase. A locker
# re-verifies an existing session; it does not admit a new one.
# Fingerprint unlock is the separate veiland-fingerprint service, run in
# parallel. If pam-auth-update's fingerprint profile is on, common-auth
# also runs pam_fprintd: with veiland's [fingerprint] enabled it usually
# fails fast (veiland's own service holds the reader) and falls through
# to the password; with it off, an attempt can wait up to 10 s.
auth     include  common-auth
